      "rationale": "Page-by-page visual inspection of the restaurant-issued dine-in menu establishes the item boundaries. Trucha Frita a la Santa Monica is described as fried trout with sauteed vegetables, rice and beans, so fish is directly supported and shellfish is not attributable to that item. Quesadilla Special is chicken quesadilla with guacamole and sour cream, directly supporting milk; shellfish and a specific wheat/gluten tortilla are not stated for that item. The separate Crab and Shrimps Quesadilla directly supports shellfish and milk from crab, shrimp and melted cheese. Gambas al Ajillo directly supports shellfish, milk, wheat and gluten from shrimp sauteed in garlic butter and served with bread. The two prose-only frozen description rows are duplicate extraction artifacts and must not publish independent allergen records. This removes cross-item smear without making allergen-absence or cross-contact claims."
